# go-d: d through the Go worker, which has a go.mod of its own. An import path under the module
# go.mod names is that package's directory; q := queue.New() is typed by New's return type; a
# method called on an interface lands on the interface, and a second d lists what implements it;
# a name bound by a make( that gofmt left wrapped over three lines answers instead of a panic
# (#178); a field read on a line with a `→` before it; fmt.Errorf into GOROOT, read-only, with
# no toolchain fetched on the way (#183), named `fmt/errors.go` on the status line (#235). Tabs
# are drawn four wide, as gofmt means them.
merl worker/main.go
wait func main() {
key t /
type New(
key Enter d
wait New: via import worker/internal/queue/
key [ /
type Push
key Enter d
wait Push → memQueue.Push (via queue.New() *memQueue)
key [ /
type Pop
key Enter d
wait Pop → Queue.Pop (via q: Queue)
key d
wait Pop: implementations of Queue.Pop, 2 declarations (2/2)
key Escape [
wait worker/main.go  33:22
key /
type jobs, job
key Enter d
wait jobs → drain.jobs (local)
key [ /
type Kind)
key Enter d
wait Kind → Job.Kind (via job: Job)
key [ /
type Errorf
key Enter d
wait Errorf: via import fmt
